Align indirect callback function signatures with their caller typedefs under Fil-C

Fil-C enforces exact argument count/size and return type matching at
indirect call sites. Align PHP 7.0 callbacks with PHP 8 signatures:

- sapi/cli/php_cli.c: static void print_extension_info(zend_extension *ext)
- sapi/fpm/fpm/fpm_main.c: static void print_extension_info(zend_extension *ext)
  with zend_llist_apply()
- sapi/cgi/cgi_main.c: static void print_extension_info(zend_extension *ext)
  with zend_llist_apply()
- sapi/phpdbg/phpdbg_prompt.c: static void add_zendext_info(zend_extension *ext)
- Zend/zend_builtin_functions.c: static void add_zendext_info(zend_extension *ext, void *arg)
- ext/libxml/libxml.c: static void _php_libxml_free_error(xmlErrorPtr error)
- ext/gd/libgd/gd_jpeg.c: static void php_jpeg_emit_message(j_common_ptr jpeg_info, int level)

